  "narrative": "All due discovery results were assessed using the signed convention: for direction -1 claims positive signed estimates mean exposed lines have stronger dependency, and for direction +1 claims positive signed estimates mean weaker dependency. The 0.15 composite-score threshold was applied with attention to interval uncertainty. H306/R301 accepts KEAP1-loss weaker dependency among low-aneuploidy lines (+0.810; lower bound 0.730), a large localization outside high aneuploidy but still discovery-only because validation budget is exhausted. H308/R302 accepts SMARCA4-loss stronger dependency among low-aneuploidy lines (+0.824; lower bound 0.747). H309/R303 accepts TP53-loss weaker dependency among low-aneuploidy lines (+0.415; lower bound 0.299). H99/R306 accepts SMARCA4-loss stronger dependency when RNA omics are absent (+0.749; lower bound 0.531), supporting robustness across omics availability despite smaller cells. H162/R308, H171/R309, and H172/R310 accept MSI-high stronger dependency in hypoxia and relaxed screen-quality contexts (+0.785, +0.841, and +0.820; lower bounds 0.495, 0.632, and 0.549). H89/R305 rejects ARID1A-loss within SMARCA4-loss lines (-0.051; interval -0.205 to 0.103). H84/R311 rejects the HUMAGNE_CD library contrast (-0.063; interval -0.201 to 0.075). H119/R312 rejects SMARCA4-loss modification by high research_signature_c (+0.042; interval -0.148 to 0.233). H307/R304 remains unresolved but closed because PTEN-loss in high-Cas9, SMARCA4-wildtype, 10% serum is directionally supportive (+0.200), yet its lower bound is below threshold (0.056). H160/R307 remains unresolved but closed because CDKN2A-loss in a clean low-aneuploidy background is directionally supportive (+0.162), yet its lower bound is below threshold (0.054). No validation was requested because no voluntary validation requests remain. These conclusions remain observational dataset-specific associations; eligibility and subgroup conditioning may induce selection or collider-like structure, multiplicity remains high, and the results do not establish causal knockout effects or generalizable biological mechanisms.",
  "research_notes": "Final appraise at iteration 25. No validation requests remain. Key new acceptances: KEAP1-loss low-aneuploidy weaker dependency R301 (+0.810 lower 0.730), SMARCA4-loss low-aneuploidy stronger dependency R302 (+0.824 lower 0.747), TP53-loss low-aneuploidy weaker dependency R303 (+0.415 lower 0.299), SMARCA4-loss without RNA omics R306 (+0.749 lower 0.531), and MSI-high hypoxia or lower-quality screens R308-R310 (+0.785/+0.841/+0.820). Key rejections: ARID1A-loss within SMARCA4-loss R305, HUMAGNE_CD library R311, and SMARCA4 x research_signature_c interaction R312. Key unresolved: PTEN high-Cas9 clean 10% serum R304 (+0.200 lower 0.056) and CDKN2A clean low-aneuploidy R307 (+0.162 lower 0.054). Overall final pattern: SMARCA4-loss robust strongest-dependency association; MSI-high robust stronger-dependency; TP53-loss robust weaker-dependency; KEAP1-loss very large discovery-only weaker-dependency, now localized in low aneuploidy as well as high aneuploidy; PTEN-loss moderate overall association with several cleaner localizations but many context-specific intervals not threshold precise; CDKN2A remains a narrow candidate with limited precision; technical and constructed assay contrasts generally null. Audit: high multiplicity, ROC eligibility and conditioning on omics, Cas9, growth, ploidy, lineage, media, batch, and genetic exclusions can induce selection or collider-like associations; no claims should be treated as causal or generalizable without external replication."
